# Test: ? on a highlighted COMMAND candidate opens the box on its explanation
# VALIDATES: AC-9 and AC-11 for a command -- the box holds the declared ze:help,
#   which is a different text from the summary the row holds. Both are on the
#   screen at once, and neither repeats the other.
# PREVENTS: the box repeating the one-line summary, which leaves the long
#   explanation unreachable from the interactive CLI.
#
# The path: ? -> revealCandidateExplanation -> revealExplanationOf ->
# CommandCompleter.Explain -> revealDeclared (internal/component/cli/model_keys.go).

option=timeout:value=30s

# go.mod marker: ze-test editor roots its base dir at the first go.mod above
# the working directory, so --dir . resolves to this test's temp dir.
tmpfs=go.mod:terminator=EOF_MOD
module ze-ui-command-help-explanation-box-fixture
EOF_MOD

tmpfs=command-help-explanation-box.et:terminator=EOF_ET
# Test: the explanation of a command candidate reaches the box, and the summary stays on the row
option=mode:value=command
option=timeout:value=10s

# "clear dns cache " has two children, so Tab opens the menu on the first one,
# record. Nothing is explained yet.
input=type:text=clear dns cache
input=key:name=space
input=tab
expect=dropdown:visible
expect=explanation:empty

# ? explains the highlighted candidate. The box takes the ze:help of
# clear dns cache record, which states what an unknown type does. Its
# description says nothing about that, so this sentence can only come from the
# long text.
input=type:text=?
expect=explanation:contains=An unknown type is reported inside the answer rather than as an error.

# The row still holds the summary while the box holds the explanation, so the
# two texts are on the screen together and neither is a copy of the other.
expect=hint:contains=Evict DNS cache entries for one record name, or one name and type when a type is provided.
EOF_ET

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test editor --dir . --all
expect=exit:code=0
